  "live_records": {
    "q-217265": {
      "dom_id": "step-q217265",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The solution to $\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{4q}$ is$\\,\\,q\\,=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $q=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{4q} \\\\ 1\\cdot 4q & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\ 4q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4q & =2 \\\\ \\frac{4q}{4} & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\ q & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $q=\\frac{1}{2}$ is different from $q=0,$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $q=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
