    "q-217287": {
      "dom_id": "step-q217287",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The solution to $\\frac{2s}{4s+3}=\\frac{2}{5}$  is$\\,\\,s\\,=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the denominator $4s+3$ cannot be zero, since division by $0$ is undefined. Therefore we cannot have $4s+3=0,$ which means $s=-\\frac{3}{4}$ cannot be a solution.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2s}{4s+3} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2s\\cdot 5 & =(4s+3)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 10s & =8s+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10s & =8s+6 \\\\ 10s-8s & =8s+6-8s \\\\ 2s & =6 \\\\ s & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $s=3$ is different from $s=-\\frac{3}{4}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $s=3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
          "dom_index": 0,
          "disabled": false,
          "input_html": "<div id=\"freeResponseTextbox-1\" class=\"matheditor-wrapper-answer\" ;=\"\" style=\"min-width:30px;\n                                        margin-left:2px;\n                                        margin-right:1px;\n                                        background:;\"><div class=\"mq-editable-field mq-math-mode\" style=\"border: none; outline: none;\"><span class=\"mq-textarea\"><textarea autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\"true\" style=\"\" disabled=\"\"></textarea></span><span class=\"mq-root-block\" mathquill-block-id=\"31\"><span mathquill-command-id=\"33\">3</span></span></div></div>",
